  m_text: " Tennessee is known for having one of the richest cave systems in the
    United States, with thousands of documented caves. The state\u2019s karst landscape,
    made of soluble limestone and dolomite, creates ideal conditions for cave formation.
    Over millions of years, underground rivers carved out chambers, tunnels, and
    caverns that continue to evolve today. These caves attract scientists, explorers,
    and tourists from across the country. Their natural beauty and geological significance
    make them one of Tennessee\u2019s most fascinating natural features.\n\nOne of
    the most famous caves in Tennessee is Ruby Falls, located deep inside Lookout
    Mountain. Ruby Falls is home to the tallest and deepest underground waterfall
    open to the public in the nation. Visitors travel by elevator into the mountain,
    then walk through narrow passageways decorated with stunning rock formations.
    The waterfall itself is illuminated with dramatic lighting to highlight its height
    and power. This cave is both a geological "
