  m_text: "wonder and a key tourist attraction.\n\n Another notable cave is Cumberland
    Caverns, one of the longest caves in Tennessee. It features massive chambers,
    shimmering cave formations, and underground lakes. Cumberland Caverns also hosts
    concerts known as \u201CBluegrass Underground,\u201D creating a unique blend
    of music and geology. The cave\u2019s expansive size allows for long tours that
    showcase its varied terrain. Its blend of entertainment and natural beauty makes
    it one of the state\u2019s most memorable cave experiences.\n\n Tennessee\u2019s
    caves also play an essential role in local ecosystems. Bats, salamanders, and
    rare cave-dwelling insects rely on these dark environments for survival. Some
    species are endemic, meaning they are found nowhere else in the world. The stable
    temperatures and humidity within caves create ideal living conditions for these
    creatures. Protecting these habitats is a significant responsibility for "
